    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13619" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-vīto</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to avoid, go out of the way of, shun</i>
			(rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illos fluctus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 1, 2, 79</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">procellam temporis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 1, 3, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 3, 5, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">letum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					3, 1092</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolorem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 2, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exiguum censum turpemque repulsam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 1, 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suspicionem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 11</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσφημίαν</span> nominis, <i><span class="en">id.
				Aug. 92</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stultitiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Eccl. 2, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
